  ('rc4088-rev23', '1599', 'Total current assets', 'Current assets', true, false, 'depreciation is referred to as amortization of tangible assets, depletion is referred to as amortization of natural resource assets, and amortization is referred to as amortization of intangible assets. Total tangible capital assets, represents the sum of all tangible capital assets reported, and item 2009 – Total accumulated amortization of tangible capital assets, represents the sum of all the accumulated amortization of the tangible capital assets reported, within items 1600 to 1922. When reporting this breakdown, do not show the net final amount of the tangible capital assets on the GIFI. However, if your financial statements show an amount, for example fixed assets (net), for which there is no breakdown, report it under item 2008 – Total tangible capital assets.'),
